{"title":"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e055135d74cf1398148a3832f952eb0730bd23d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=340$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/973c3f80d65986408c1c1dff17bd75f53e0abc45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=146$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a1086fcb54dab3b6d76fdcdb37bab28e91bdd60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA=390$\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is a point on the interior of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> such that the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, then the average of all distinct possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1ec98d653e92241491489b63d512a898317539d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac pq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170200756543596efeb46fca1cf29a617e8c9192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b384cbecaa595bc5afa5a24f722a8887611cc7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(3.5cm); defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)); pair A,B,C,M; A=dir(95); B=dir(-117); C=dir(-63); M=(2B+3C)/5;  draw(A--B--C--A); draw(A--M,dashed); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); dot(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NW); label(&quot;$340$&quot;,A--B,W); label(&quot;$390$&quot;,A--C,E); label(&quot;$146$&quot;,B--C,S); [/asy]\" width=\"102\" height=\"168\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer and that it lies on the interior of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, the shortest possible length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is the length of the altitude dropped straight down from vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. This can be calculated as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edc54a3a69e46d191bf7226cd1a996f3b9c5a3f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2[\\triangle ABC]}{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b8e2a396e6068718549901c58451f6a39ad8e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2[\\triangle ABC]}{146}\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"39\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/765bdd4c99cf7ccb5d661dfb4afe099fb09e5d17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[\\triangle ABC]}{73}.\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"38\" /> The area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> can be found using Heron's formula. It is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/623ccfce0dfafe401f04cef9c752a9b3c2e9448d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}=\\sqrt{438 \\cdot 98 \\cdot 292 \\cdot 48}=24528.\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"32\" /> The shortest possible length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/8829b98774f1597d278cc095f02f3ad8985bee65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{24528}{73}=336.\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> can be anything greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2d0937b35e43b1d504a7197abe9c3560a3a856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$336$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, but the condition that point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> lies in the interior of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> limits the values that we can reach. Starting at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and heading east (we cannot get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea83521b9e585be335f2a1db9eafb6e4cfe19b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$340$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), we reach the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a8e01538310ba9bf6e53b4dd562d0122fec6e69.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AM=339, 338, 337, 336,\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"16\" /> and then as we move further east the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> will start to increase. We then reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e50e90aac731ddd0cc999e57cc726bf5490e740f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AM=337, 338, 339, 340,..., 386, 387, 388, 389.\\]\" width=\"358\" height=\"16\" /> We cannot get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/172bf264a8b2c082be7f24b12296b09faaa2dfff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$390$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> because then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e76eeae26796bb8b10b09293c8c4c7c2cc009d44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=C$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> which is not allowed. The distinct possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/7/6e7ba3739a38c01a597ad1837f3adc8eccf2c213.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[336, 337, 338,..., 388, 389.\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"16\" /> The average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/630f7efe28c48c60cdb1e5725a3a4a085cec5031.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{336+389}{2}=\\frac{725}{2}.\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"37\" /> The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8bd458df5b8c2758d2bb983c54a5fea76c61ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$725+2=\\boxed{727}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II\" title=\"2020 CIME II\">2020 CIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 CIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIME II Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"CIME Problems and Solutions\"> All CIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:MAC_Notice&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:MAC Notice (page does not exist)\">Template:MAC Notice</a